cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite it and the paper it accompanies once published."
title: "DAIM-OS Distributed Execution Artifact: Independently Executing Per-Switch Cores, Explicit State Semantics, and a Statistically Validated Evaluation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Banjar
    given-names: Ameen
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0871-5153"
version: 1.2.1
date-released: 2026-08-13
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ameen-banjar/daim-os-distributed-execution"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21924571"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility artifact for "Distributing the DAIM-OS Table-and-Signal
  Contract: Independently Executing Per-Switch Cores, Explicit State
  Semantics, and a Statistically Validated Evaluation" (Paper 2 in the DAIM
  six-paper programme). Contains four new C modules extending the
  reconstructed DAIM Core (from the companion Packet-In artifact) with a
  distributed host-location state table, a peer wire protocol, a persistent
  peer transport, and a distributed learning application; the Python gate
  and statistical-campaign harnesses for eight mechanism gates (propagation,
  duplicate/stale/epoch-ordering rejection, node-failure isolation,
  partition detection/reconvergence, node-count scaling to 32, and
  ownership-conflict detection), each demonstrated as a single trial and
  independently repeated 30 times against three explicit baselines
  (single-Core, no-exchange, distributed/versioned); and the full raw
  per-repetition evidence, gate/campaign result summaries, and manifests
  with SHA-256 checksums.
keywords:
  - distributed systems
  - software-defined networking
  - state dissemination
  - OpenFlow
  - Open vSwitch
  - reproducible systems research
  - concurrency
